id: pmc-agent-contract-drift
title: Index declared agent contract changes across releases
description: "Read-only version interval index over explicit stable agent-behavior obligations; preserve additions, removals, changes, evidence and unchanged references without prose inference."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T03:29:59.126Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T08:36:25.361Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Unchanged contracts collapse to references; Added, removed and changed obligations remain distinct; A ten-release fixture returns all relevant changes in fewer bytes than concatenated notes"
comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T03:30:10.766Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core sdk/cli-contracts describes the installed CLI; audience-contracts publishes release-local prose and consumer-upgrades compiles explicit breaking actions. Sibling pm-ts-starter sdk-contracts compiles consumers across SDK versions; pm-evidence audits claims. None indexes persistent package-declared agent obligations over releases. Add stable obligations on agent-behavior facets; legacy prose produces explicit omissions. Reuse listAllComplete, status registry roles and generator release/closure selection. This feature adds no import, sync, journal, lock or tracker write path. commitWorkspaceTransaction does not isolate ordinary SDK writers (pm-cli#1620); no isolation claim is made."
  "2026-10-29T03:34:18.014Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the read-only SDK and drift command: baseline at from; transitions through to; explicit tombstones; provenance-only repeats collapse to definition references; conflicts in one release refuse. Strict declaration producer/parser is shared with output definition validation. Legacy prose and individual invalid declarations become omissions without suppressing valid siblings. Targeted verification covers SDK/host/standalone in a non-git tracker, extreme numeric and sparse-array inputs, and 500 seeded native-state replay sequences. Documentation records the non-atomic read/settings window and makes no transaction isolation claim."
  "2026-10-29T03:38:09.138Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable non-git copy only, replacing buildAgentContractDrift with an empty report makes the ten-release regression fail with ERR_ASSERTION; fixed=1 pass, reverted=1 fail, restored=1 pass. The source worktree was never reverted. Ten-release evidence: 5 transitions, 16 unchanged references, 4 definitions; JSON 2661 bytes and TOON 2814 bytes versus 13982 bytes concatenated notes. Real public origin/main tracker validation: 206 items, 0 declared agent facets, 0 transitions/omissions, JSON 144 bytes, TOON 129 bytes, all notes 35931 bytes; SDK/CLI equal with git absent; all 422 source files unchanged (manifest SHA256 59b9f1053be14fe1d941b2abb1e6231b3e7dc8e306e1b5e16c58f8f603d57689). This is explicitly zero-declaration real-data evidence; nonempty behavior is proved by the ten-release fixture, not inferred from old prose."
  "2026-10-29T03:44:06.350Z",codex-agent,"Seed 0x6dc1f7 completed all 500 model sequences (1500 SDK updates including older-input replays), comparing native state read back through the SDK, canonicalDocument body normalization, relationship preservation, explicit unset scope under random ambient focus, custom status roles/aliases and JSON/TOON round trips. The focused run passed 6/6 before the separate aggregate-budget regression was added (3/3 budget, fixture and output regressions then passed). Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (246 declarations), package allowlist/content scan (99 files, zero failures) pass. Linked behavioral-revert test ran through pinned pm test with progress and passed; test result tracking is disabled by project policy, so the command receipt is recorded here. Full release gates are delegated to CI under npm and Bun at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T03:46:13.484Z",codex-agent,"Final targeted boundary coverage: agent-contract-drift.ts and agent-contract-command.ts each measure 100% lines, branches and functions at unchanged thresholds (6 focused cases); the 500-sequence model passed separately, and the command-set/status-filter regression passed 1/1. Aggregate budgets include facets plus declarations to bound omission output. No import/apply/sync path or journal state is introduced. Existing native changelog exporter and packed launcher checks remain exercised in CI; packed acceptance now includes 32 drift checks across 8 launchers and 6 install modes. Changelog generation and link checks pass. Remaining limits: public tracker has no structured agent declarations; read plus settings is not an atomic snapshot; statement coverage is not independently measured by the existing repository gate."
  "2026-10-29T03:55:42.261Z",codex-agent,"Fixture quality refinement: replaced repeated placeholder prose with release-specific notes listing the actual declared obligations, affected commands and evidence. The same ten releases still retain all 5 transitions, 16 unchanged references and 4 definitions; JSON 2661 bytes and TOON 2814 bytes now compare against 3832 bytes of substantive concatenated notes. Behavioral revert proof rerun: fixed passes, empty-index function fails, restored passes. Test typecheck passes. Initial-head CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40814142585 is still in lifecycle validation; the fixture-only follow-up requires fresh exact-head CI, with final results reported on the PR."
  "2026-10-29T03:59:11.164Z",codex-agent,"Added independent seed 0x9a71c: 500 randomly generated custom status registries, with randomized role assignments and alias spellings, publish exactly the done-role contracts and round-trip through both encodings. This and the substantive ten-release fixture passed 2/2; test typecheck passes. Final compression evidence remains JSON 2661 bytes and TOON 2814 bytes versus 3832 bytes concatenated notes. The separate 500-sequence / 1500-update SDK state model already passed. All final tracker writes precede the fresh exact-head CI run; no item is closed."
  "2026-10-29T04:18:31.941Z",codex-agent,"CI handoff at the queue-rule 30-minute cutoff: commit b276a2d lifecycle passed in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40815373426 (GraphQL-confirmed). That lifecycle runs the behavioral revert, read-only public tracker validation and packed acceptance with asserted totals of 318 checks, including 32 drift checks across 6 installation modes and 8 launchers. Node 22 and Node 26 matrix jobs are queued; 0 of 4 planned full npm/Bun release gates have completed, so full-gate test counts and package-wide coverage remain pending. CodeQL, Semgrep and DeepScan passed on that head. GitHub REST quota prevents detailed log access; GraphQL status still works. This tracker-only checkpoint starts fresh exact-head CI; the PR carries the final run link. Keep the item in progress, release only this agent claim, do not merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T05:06:11.285Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1 resumed on a clean worktree at 497f4c3. origin/main is already an ancestor (3 branch-only commits, 0 behind), so no merge is needed. Fixing two classes: producer/formatter closure under provenance aggregation, and release-scope isolation before facet validation or budget accounting. Audit all package builders, commands, encodings and packed consumers; preserve valid input and individual omissions. Add adversarial/property regressions and per-function behavioral revert proofs in disposable copies, then exact-head npm/Bun CI gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-29T05:18:27.895Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed. Producer/formatter closure: evidence unions can contain 64 times the record budget; root-level plus record-level omissions can exceed the record budget; native SDK IDs must not acquire a formatter-only 1024-byte cap. Derived output bounds from the input domain, retained native ID strings, used Sets to avoid quadratic merge/sort, and preserved every orphan contributor coordinate. Temporal isolation: drift checked future releases after validating facets, and consumer upgrades invoked unbounded audience validation before checking to. Both now use shared numeric-release selection before facet validation; bounded audience SDK selection requires release grouping and default unbounded behavior is unchanged. Other public output builders (audience, upgrades, claims, milestones and corrections) have no smaller post-aggregation formatter cap; milestone/correction storage integrity validation is separate from release projection. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied in the orchestrator report or PR review records. New focused suite passes 5/5, including 100032 evidence IDs, 150000 omissions, 500 future variants and actual non-git SDK/host/standalone parity; JSON and TOON round-trip with native state unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T05:28:01.140Z",codex-agent,"Function-only behavioral revert proof completed against reviewed commit 497f4c3 in disposable source copies: reverting formatAgentContractDrift fails the aggregate-evidence/omission producer-closure tests; reverting buildAgentContractDrift fails temporal isolation and contributor coordinates; reverting buildAudienceContracts fails the shared bounded-release property; reverting buildConsumerUpgrades fails the upgrade scope property. Each mutant ran with all other fixed functions unchanged, failed with ERR_ASSERTION, and passed again after restoration. Pure tests import src, so these checks do not rely on stale dist. All four fixed and restored controls passed, plus the original empty-index revert proof. Targeted compatibility covered 24 executed cases; five affected modules each measured 100% lines, branches and functions. The new 500-variant scope property also includes valid future actions that conflict with historical definitions, and verifies every adversarial variant was exercised. Existing tests are preserved; long native-state models run in the full CI npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-29T05:32:03.611Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 300 passed all 5 new adversarial tests (zero failures/skips); project policy disables automatic result tracking, so this receipt is preserved in the comment. An added sixth test checks that arrays beyond the derived output limits still refuse in both encodings, so the fix widens to the producer domain without removing bounds. Typecheck/test typecheck/docstring lint pass (248 declarations); package allowlist and content scan pass for 103 files. Refreshed read-only public origin/main validation: 206 items, zero declared agent facets, zero omissions, JSON 144 bytes, TOON 129 bytes, all-notes 35931 bytes, all 422 files unchanged, SDK/CLI equal, warm SDK 2911 ms. The same manifest SHA256 59b9f1053be14fe1d941b2abb1e6231b3e7dc8e306e1b5e16c58f8f603d57689 is retained. Packed acceptance now asserts 334 checks: the existing 32 drift checks include 100032 merged evidence IDs, and 16 added upgrade checks exclude malformed future metadata across all 8 launchers / 6 install modes. Both full npm/Bun release gates remain unchanged and run in CI with at most two test workers."
  "2026-10-29T05:39:40.940Z",codex-agent,"Superseded-head full CI completed with 947/948 passing under each Node matrix leg: the missing drift entry in the standalone help/parser inventory caused one assertion failure and 99.97% aggregate branch coverage (CLI 99.65%). This was not approval. Closed the help-contract class too: inventory now includes drift, root synopsis validation derives every non-root/non-audit command from the parser map, and all actions of each command contribute their advertised flags. Completed drift root help and the corrections shared help flag, preserving parser behavior. Added printHelp to the function-only behavioral revert runner. The queued 26e2aad run was canceled as superseded; the next push gets fresh exact-head full gates."
  "2026-10-29T05:42:45.789Z",codex-agent,"Help class repair verified: all 11 parser/help tests pass, including every command synopsis and every accepted flag. Restoring only printHelp from 497f4c3 fails the new synopsis assertions; fixed and restored controls pass. The complete revert runner now passes all five function-only mutants plus the original empty-index proof. Source/test typechecks and docstring lint pass; no existing assertion or coverage threshold was removed or weakened. Final full gates execute through the unchanged CI release:check commands, each limited to two test workers."
  "2026-10-29T05:50:40.014Z",codex-agent,"Final verifier hardening passed: six independent behavioral reverts in five functions (producer bounds, drift scope, orphan provenance, audience scope, upgrade scope, and parser/help agreement) all fail their adversarial assertions; every fixed/restored control passes. The original empty-index proof also passes. Reverts mutate only the selected function in disposable copies. The runner is now self-contained and does not require a retained review commit or git history, so squash merges and archived source checkouts cannot break CI verification. No product behavior changed in this verifier adjustment. Help tests also passed 11/11 through pinned pm test with progress. Claim is released, item remains in progress, and unchanged full npm/Bun CI gates follow the next push."
  "2026-10-29T06:07:28.452Z",codex-agent,"Repair handoff at the existing 30-minute CI cutoff: ed9ddca run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40825925537 remains in lifecycle validation; 0/4 full npm/Bun gate executions have completed. CodeQL, Semgrep and DeepScan passed on that head. Packed acceptance is configured for 334 checks (32 large-evidence drift checks plus 16 temporal-isolation upgrade checks across 8 launchers / 6 install modes) but its current-run result is not yet confirmed. Both supplied blockers and the discovered help-contract failure are fixed, with related bounds/native-ID/orphan cases covered. Local evidence: 36 targeted cases passed across runs, 7 detected behavioral reverts including the original feature proof, all fixed/restored controls pass, five affected contract modules at 100% L/B/F, 103-file package scan clean, public tracker 206 items and 422 unchanged files. Existing tests and full thresholds remain intact. This tracker-only checkpoint triggers fresh exact-head CI; the PR records its final run link. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification; do not merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T06:27:24.430Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: general rule is to compare release identity after normalizing the presentation heading through the same grammar the generator emits, before reading any excluded facets. The worktree is clean and origin/main is already an ancestor, so no merge is required. Auditing every release-bound consumer, SDK/CLI formatter, release-window fixture and packed launcher. Prior full CI remains pending; previous successful targeted work is retained. No additional non-blocking defect was supplied in this round."
  "2026-10-29T06:30:23.337Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class audit: all temporal contract predicates, drift observation identity and upgrade ledger attribution now reuse generator normalizeReleaseHeadingKey through one parseContractReleaseHeading helper. Strict bare-version input parsing remains separate. Searched all release.heading, ledger release, releaseWindows, version comparisons and command paths; ordinary generation already owns the shared heading normalizer, while the three report builders were the affected class. Original headings remain in audience attribution. Added a seeded 500-case corpus covering plain, dated, prefixed, bracketed, linked and whitespace headings, good and bad future facets, in-range refusal, legacy compatibility, unbounded publication and both formats. Added dated future metadata to the real non-git SDK/host/standalone test and every packed npm/Bun launcher; captured-archive SDK acceptance now also exercises bounded dated releaseWindows. No other actionable review finding exists in the supplied review or inline comments."
  "2026-10-29T06:33:45.668Z",codex-agent,"The package-wide audit also found a second heading parser in generator sectionVersionKey, used by sinceVersion lower bounds. It handled plain dated headings but disagreed on bracketed presentation; it now delegates to the same generator normalizer while retaining the existing release-key normalization and Unreleased behavior. The 500-case test checks lower and upper bounds together. The first expanded revert run correctly produced invalid_facets under the reverted predicate; the proof harness requires assertion failures, so the new test now explicitly asserts that bounded generation does not throw. The production fix was unchanged by that test-harness correction."
  "2026-10-29T06:34:43.925Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 verification: 26 focused contract compatibility/adversarial cases passed with node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-skip-pattern=\"500 model-based|500 seeded SDK-read\" --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=src/contract-versions.ts --test-coverage-include=src/audience-contracts.ts --test-coverage-include=src/consumer-upgrades.ts test/agent-contract-drift.test.ts test/audience-contracts.test.ts test/consumer-upgrades.test.ts test/contract-report-closure.test.ts. Those three modules measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Existing long SDK models remain preserved for full CI. Six generator limit/visibility cases passed with node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"since-version|limitSections|visibility narrowing\" test/enhancements.test.ts test/generator-coverage.test.ts. The new heading property also passes through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 120. Typecheck, build, test typecheck, docstrings and 103-member package allowlist passed. No full-gate success is claimed yet."
  "2026-10-29T06:34:44.789Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts passes in a disposable source copy. Each of five new function-only reverts (isContractReleaseAfter, parseContractReleaseHeading, sectionVersionKey, drift observation and upgrade attribution) makes the 500-case heading property fail an assertion, and every fixed/restored control passes. All seven existing reverts remain, for 12 detected faulty behaviors and 24 passing control runs total. Mutation restoration uses finally; no git history dependency. No existing test was weakened or deleted. Packed acceptance now expects 336 checks including two captured-archive SDK dated-window encoding checks, plus dated/bracketed future native metadata across all eight npm/Bun launchers; full CI will measure that result."
  "2026-10-29T06:41:47.752Z",codex-agent,"CI handoff before final verification: product head 55c5016 is in lifecycle validation at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40830104388; currently 0/4 full npm/Bun release gates have completed. The existing 30-minute cutoff is 07:05 UTC and will not reset after this tracker-only checkpoint. Superseded runs 40827622638 and 40825925537 were canceled to free runners, not counted as approvals. All tracker writes and own-claim release are now complete before final-head CI verification. The PR and final report will give the fresh checkpoint run URL and measured results; current 336-check acceptance remains pending. Existing real-data evidence is retained without redoing finished work: public read-only scratch tracker, 206 items, zero declared agent facets, 422 files unchanged, JSON 144 bytes and TOON 129 bytes versus 35931 note bytes. Remaining limits are pending CI and the documented non-atomic SDK read/settings window."
  "2026-10-29T08:20:35.738Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: origin/main was one commit ahead and has been merged first (toolchain updates only; no item/history conflict). General rule: every accepted stored release spelling must normalize through the generator identity normalizer before numeric validation or temporal comparison; strict option parsing must not silently narrow persisted input compatibility. Auditing padded calendar, numeric and daily-suffix release identities across all three report builders, generator placement/bounds, SDK/CLI, both encodings, packed consumers and non-git trackers. The previous bbcc097 CI is now fully green, including both npm and Bun gates on Node 22 and 26; those are prior-head results, not approval for this repair. No additional non-blocking finding was supplied."
  "2026-10-29T08:22:59.306Z",codex-agent,"The merged package pin is pm 2026.10.26 and dependencies are now installed from the updated lockfile before further tracker writes. Initial claim/start attempts using the pre-install 2026.10.25 runtime were refused; its comment command unexpectedly accepted the progress comment. No stale-runtime override was used, and that append-only comment is retained. This upstream guard inconsistency is report-only under the queue rules. The repair will make normalizeReleaseHeadingKey reuse the existing normalizeReleaseKey function, fixing numeric identity at the shared source rather than adding a second zero-padding parser."
  "2026-10-29T08:28:21.729Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed: normalizeReleaseKey already owns zero-padding identity for release placement, suppressed releases, attribution and lower bounds. normalizeReleaseHeadingKey now delegates to it after extracting heading decoration. That one shared function feeds drift baselines/transitions, upper-bound facet exclusion, upgrade attribution, generator sectionVersionKey, and existing Markdown replacement/insertion; compareVersionStrings already compares padded numeric segments numerically. Added an independent 500-case model with known canonical versions, random padding on each segment, daily suffixes, aliases, dates/brackets/links, valid/malformed future facets, inclusive bounds and both encodings. It also checks replacing padded/unpadded headings in both directions without duplicating a release. Strict new range inputs and unsafe/prerelease refusals stay covered. The new native test uses IDs returned by SDK create (no handwritten prefix normalization) and malformed future array records accepted by the native schema; its initial fixture-shape and bare-ID assumptions were corrected without changing production behavior or weakening any existing test."
  "2026-10-29T08:36:13.427Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 checks passed: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-skip-pattern=\"500 model-based|500 seeded SDK-read\" --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=src/contract-versions.ts --test-coverage-include=src/audience-contracts.ts --test-coverage-include=src/consumer-upgrades.ts test/agent-contract-drift.test.ts test/audience-contracts.test.ts test/consumer-upgrades.test.ts test/contract-report-closure.test.ts passed 28/28; those three modules measured 100% lines/branches/functions. node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"release attribution|padded/unpadded|since-version|limitSections|prepend|backfill|bracket|heading\" test/enhancements.test.ts test/generator-coverage.test.ts passed 28/28. The two new padding cases also passed through pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 120; project result tracking remains disabled by policy, so this comment preserves the receipt. npm run build, typecheck, build:test, docstring, pack:dry-run and pack:scan passed; both pack checks measured 103 files with zero failures. Original 500-sequence native models remain for full CI, not re-run locally."
  "2026-10-29T08:36:18.289Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof passed: node scripts/prove-agent-contract-drift-revert.ts restores only the reviewed normalizeReleaseHeadingKey implementation in a disposable source copy; the new 500-case padding property fails an assertion, and fixed/restored controls pass. All 12 earlier regressions remain detected: 13 behavioral reverts, 26 passing controls total. No existing test was weakened or deleted; no Git history dependency or active-worktree mutation. Packed acceptance now expects 382 checks, preserving all previous 336 and adding six archive-SDK calendar encodings plus 40 calendar launcher/state checks across npm/Bun global/local and npx/bunx. Full npm and Bun release gates will run in CI with at most two test workers and unchanged thresholds. Prior bbcc097 run 40830869972 passed all four gates (958 tests each, 100% L/B/F); that remains prior-head evidence only."
